WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.000
It's been a few years since Disney's Frozen
burst onto the screen, so we wouldn't blame

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.400
you if you've let go some of the finer details
of the plot.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.600
Fortunately, we've gathered together everything
you need to know before heading to the theater

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.760
for the sequel.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.680
Originally conceived as a loose retelling
of the Hans Christian Andersen tale "The Snow

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:23.820
Queen," the initial vision for Frozen looked
a lot different than the movie Disney wound

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.720
up releasing.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:30.380
In the original script, Elsa was an indisputable
villain, she and Anna weren't sisters or even

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:36.050
royalty, and the story culminated in a climactic
battle featuring an army of snow monsters

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.940
and a devastating avalanche.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:43.500
However, director Chris Buck and writer, and
eventual co-director, Jennifer Lee realized

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.700
something was missing, and decided to make
its two central characters sisters instead

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:49.760
of strangers.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.700
"Do you wanna build a snowman?"

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.899
The final piece of the Frozen puzzle fell
into place when songwriters Kristen Anderson-Lopez

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:04.760
and Robert Lopez wrote their first song that
would make it into the finished film, "Let

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:05.500
It Go."

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.539
After hearing the song, Lee and Buck realized
they couldn't keep Elsa a villain, and rewrote

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.800
the script in order to make her more of a
conflicted co-lead.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.380
The final version of the film featured a pair
of sisters who loved each other dearly, but

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:22.180
were driven apart by Elsa's inability to control
her powers.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:27.259
This change also required the filmmakers to
reimagine the character of Olaf from a villainous

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:30.140
henchman into a lovable, goofy sidekick.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.900
C'mon…could you even imagine this guy getting
up to no good?

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:39.600
As evidenced by the original film's twisting
path to the screen, Frozen was a collaborative

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:44.039
effort between the writers, directors, and
songwriters, and wouldn't have come to exist

00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:48.060
in its current form without any one of those
specific peoples' input.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.540
Fortunately, the whole team is returning for
the sequel, albeit in slightly altered roles.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:58.400
Chris Buck is back in the co-director's chair,
as is Jennifer Lee, who was also named head

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.400
of Walt Disney Animation Studios in 2018.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:07.600
On the music front, songwriters Kristen Anderson-Lopez
and Robert Lopez are returning with 11 original

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.540
new songs for the soundtrack, and Christophe
Beck is coming back to compose the score.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:18.280
The only significant difference in the creative
team between Frozen and Frozen 2 is the screenwriters.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.640
While the original movie's script was penned
by co-director Jennifer Lee, she'll share

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.860
writing duties on the second film with Allison
Schroeder, who wrote the screenplay for 2018's

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.520
heartwarming Christopher Robin.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:35.160
Schroeder was also nominated for an Oscar
for her screenplay for 2017's Hidden Figures,

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.900
making her a strong addition to the Frozen
team.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.860
Frozen tells the tale of the two daughters
of the King and Queen of Arendelle: Elsa,

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.600
the elder sister, and Anna, the younger one.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:51.160
Although the two were close as children, they
drifted apart after their parents taught Elsa

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:56.230
that the best way to deal with her magical
icy powers was to conceal them from the world

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.080
and to repress her emotions.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.340
As a result, Elsa has isolated herself, and
only pulls further away when the King and

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.880
Queen are lost at sea.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.480
However, as the oldest daughter, it's Elsa's
duty to take up the crown, but on the day

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:14.070
of her coronation, she loses control of her
powers and flees the kingdom.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:18.990
Anna pursues her into the mountains, aided
by the ice harvester Kristoff and his trusty

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:24.400
reindeer Sven, hoping to convince Elsa to
end the sudden winter she's created in Arendelle.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.740
Convinced she can't control her powers, Elsa
accidentally freezes Anna's heart, a spell

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.360
that will slowly kill her.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.540
Dying and heartbroken, Anna returns to Arendelle,
where the sinister Hans is in the midst of

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.060
maneuvering to take control of the kingdom.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:44.100
But before he can kill Elsa and seize the
crown, Anna stops him, and her act of true

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.060
love in saving her sister thaws her heart.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:52.620
Realizing love is the key to controlling her
powers, Elsa ends the magical winter, reconciles

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.440
with Anna, and takes up her crown as Queen
of Arendelle.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:02.080
Although six years will have passed for us
between Frozen and Frozen 2, according to

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:07.100
Disney's head of animation, Becky Bresee,
the story of Frozen 2 will begin three years

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.860
after the end of the first film.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:10.960
Bresee told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.740
"It's an evolution and an expansion of the
story of Frozen, and many of the questions

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:19.780
raised in the first movie become the mysteries
that our gang are trying to solve in this

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.540
film."

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:25.760
She added that the main question of Frozen
2 will be, "Why was Elsa born with her powers?"

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.560
"Your power will only grow.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:34.920
There is beauty in it, but also great danger."

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:40.560
But for anyone worried that Frozen 2's mystery-centered
storyline will be a departure from the first

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.320
film's focus on the relationship between two
sisters, you can put your fears to rest.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:50.479
Disney's head of effects Marlon West assured
THR that the sequel is ultimately, quote,

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.100
"about two sisters trying to stay together
while the world tries to tear them apart."

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.640
That sounds like exactly what we'd hoped for
after the emotional, family-driven tale of

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:00.760
the first film.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:06.200
Based on the trailers Disney has released
for Frozen 2, we can start to piece together

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.440
some of the plot.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.379
In the beginning, all appears to be well in
Arendelle, with Queen Elsa ruling peacefully

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:15.700
over her subjects from her gently ice-frosted
castle.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:21.879
But some sort of malevolent unseen force,
manifesting as pink flames, drives the Arendellians

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.020
out of their homes.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:27.559
Determined to get to the bottom of what's
happened to them and fix it, Anna and Elsa

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.360
set off on a quest, accompanied by Kristoff,
Sven, and Olaf.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.879
While the first film focused mostly on Anna,
Elsa looks to be the main protagonist of Frozen

00:05:36.879 --> 00:05:41.259
2, as she attempts to track down the source
of a mysterious voice she hears calling to

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:41.760
her.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:46.360
She hopes to discover the source of her powers,
and through that knowledge, somehow save her

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.200
kingdom.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:52.480
The trailers also indicate that an enchanted
forest in the far north will prove to be significant

00:05:52.499 --> 00:05:57.050
to the two sisters, and possibly provide some
further clues about the backstory of their

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.040
parents.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:04.059
In discussing the story for Frozen 2, directors
Chris Buck and Jennifer Lee, together with

00:06:04.059 --> 00:06:09.629
songwriters Kristen Anderson-Lopez and Robert
Lopez, realized they still had a few big lingering

00:06:09.629 --> 00:06:12.240
questions after the events of the first film.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.460
So they set about creating a story that would
answer them.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:20.279
If the biggest question is indeed "why does
Elsa have her powers," then that leads to

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:23.880
a logical follow-up: "Why doesn't Anna have
powers?"

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:28.659
In digging into answers about the two sisters,
it becomes obvious that we really need to

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:32.900
know more about their parents, which calls
into question the circumstances surrounding

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:33.900
their deaths.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:37.960
According to Lee, although the first film
implied that the King and Queen were headed

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:43.120
away on routine business when their ship sank,
things may not all be as they appear.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:47.259
During the 2019 D23 Expo, Lee teased the question:

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:50.400
"Where were their parents really going when
that ship went down?"

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:54.940
We've been promised that the answers to all
these questions, and more, will be revealed

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.260
in Frozen 2.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:02.380
Although audiences were introduced briefly
to King Agnarr and Queen Iduna at the beginning

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:07.560
of Frozen, they died very early on in the
film's narrative, and we learned almost nothing

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.440
about them.

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:11.500
At least, nothing beyond their instructions
to Elsa:

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.020
"Conceal it."

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:14.600
"Don't feel it."

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:20.240
Agnarr and Iduna weren't given names in the
first film, and had hardly any lines; for

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.009
their all-too-short presence, the queen was
voiced by co-director Jennifer Lee, with veteran

00:07:25.009 --> 00:07:27.420
voice actor Maurice LaMarche as the king.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:32.199
For their expanded roles in Frozen 2, however,
the royal couple will be voiced by Alfred

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.280
Molina and Evan Rachel Wood.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:40.020
Judging by her two songs on the movie's soundtrack,
Iduna will have a particularly hefty role,

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:43.830
and according to Disney's press release, the
queen will begin to wonder if the answers

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.560
she seeks can be found in her own past.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.279
The press release has less to say about Agnarr,
saying only that he'll do anything protect

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.680
his daughters from harm.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:57.760
But the casting of the Golden Globe and Emmy-nominated
Molina makes it seem as though the king will

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:00.660
have a significant part to play as well.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:06.520
Joining the impressive cast for Frozen 2,
which includes nearly every major player and

00:08:06.539 --> 00:08:11.189
a few returning minor characters from the
first movie, is This is Us actor Sterling

00:08:11.189 --> 00:08:14.720
K. Brown, who will be voicing Lieutenant Destin
Mattias.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:19.500
An Arendelle soldier who's been trapped in
the Enchanted Forest for more than 30 years,

00:08:19.509 --> 00:08:22.430
Lieutenant Mattias has, according to Disney's
press release,

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:27.659
"...never forgotten his sworn duty to Arendelle,
but the arrival of Queen Elsa and discovery

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:33.360
that she has magical powers is just the first
of many challenges to his long-held beliefs."

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:38.660
Lieutenant Mattias originally traveled to
the forest to fight against the nomadic Northuldra

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:41.180
people, presumably the enemies of Arendelle.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:45.680
However, when we see him in the trailer, he
and his men appear to be standing alongside

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:50.220
the Northuldra, raising the question of whether
the animosity between the two groups was some

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:54.980
sort of misunderstanding, or whether the trailer
is simply working to mislead us.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:09:00.460
A significant theme running through the first
Frozen was about first impressions being unreliable,

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:04.900
as evidenced with both Elsa and Hans, and
we wouldn't be surprised if it carries through

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:07.720
to the sequel in an even more prominent way.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:13.120
Frozen may have had a compelling plot, but
the sequel will be broadening the scope of

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.200
the series' storytelling quite a bit.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.200
Not only will Anna and Elsa be venturing far
outside the borders of Arendelle, but they'll

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:25.740
also be meeting new people who, at least at
first glance, appear very different from them.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:30.760
Joining the cast of Frozen 2 are several members
of the Northuldra people, including their

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:35.820
leader, Yelana, the bold and brave Honeymaren,
and the eager, fun-loving Ryder.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:40.320
According to Disney's press release, Yelana
is, "fiercely protective of her family and

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:45.000
community but is known to soften when people
show an understanding of nature and their

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.000
environment."

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:51.380
Meanwhile, Frozen 2's new pair of siblings,
Honeymaren and Ryder, seem to have views that

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:56.060
could put them at odds, with Honeymaren being
"a true free spirit [who] wants nothing more

00:09:56.060 --> 00:10:01.130
than to bring peace to the Enchanted Forest,"
while Ryder "longs to embrace the world and

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:03.180
venture beyond the magical mist."

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:07.360
It'll be interesting to see how this brother
and sister pair plays against Arendelle's

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:11.750
royal sisters, and whether they'll all be
able to work together, or wind up butting

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.960
heads as only siblings can.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:20.400
While the original film introduced us to such
non-human favorites as Olaf the snowman, Sven

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:26.080
the reindeer, and a colony of trolls, Frozen
2 looks to significantly expand its roster

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:30.100
of mystical, magical, and just plain adorable
creatures.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:35.320
Nokk the water spirit can be seen in the trailer
as the watery horse that Elsa encounters in

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.160
the ocean.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:41.060
Disney's press release states that Nokk is
"a fierce warrior and guards the secrets of

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:46.100
the forest fiercely," and that to get past
it, "a person must prove they are worthy and

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:49.460
earn its respect, an almost impossible task."

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:54.290
However, based on the brief shot of Elsa riding
the water stallion in the trailer, it appears

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:57.240
as though she manages to impress Nokk somehow.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:02.640
Frozen 2 will also introduce us to Gale, a
playful wind spirit who can seemingly be seen

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.120
in the trailer tossing leaves and children
up into the air.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:11.020
In addition, there are the massive stone earth
giants who we see in the trailer towering

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.860
over the treetops of the Enchanted Forest.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:19.090
We'll also meet Bruni, a salamander who lives
in the Enchanted Forest who is fascinated

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:21.380
by Elsa's powerful ice magic.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:26.160
After Elsa spent so much of the first movie
in isolation, it'll be nice to see her make

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:28.160
a tiny new friend in this one.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:33.680
And if Josh Gad's tweets and Bruni's adorable
Japanese character poster are any indication,

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:37.880
when we finally meet Bruni on screen, we fully
expect to fall in love with the little guy

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.100
ourselves.

